          'As a young man he entered the palace as a military officer and rose to command the guard under Lê Long Đĩnh. In 1009 the king died, leaving a small child. The official Đào Cam Mộc and the monk Vạn Hạnh persuaded the court to make Lý Công Uẩn king. The story goes that Vạn Hạnh had earlier read a prophecy on a lightning-struck kapok tree, predicting that the Lê would fall and the Lý would rise.',
