          'Đô Temple, also called the Temple of the Eight Lý Emperors, at Đình Bảng honours eight Lý kings. Local tradition holds that its core was built right after Lý Thái Tổ died in 1028, but the present buildings result from a reconstruction begun in the late 1980s. The temple is therefore evidence of long remembrance, not a surviving piece of Lý architecture.',
